## TIẾNG ANH · 16:30–17:00 — Thứ Hai: Daily standup

> *"Morning. This week is authentication, written from scratch. I want to say up front that I know rolling your own auth is usually the wrong call for a commercial product — I'm doing it to understand what the libraries are doing for me.*
> *Today: password hashing with argon2, registration, login, and access token signing. Two things I want to highlight.*
> *First, I always run the hash even when the email doesn't exist. If you return early, the response for a non-existent account is a hundred milliseconds faster, and an attacker can time that and enumerate your users. I measured both paths and they're within a few milliseconds.*
> *Second, the access token is fifteen minutes and it can't be revoked — there's no list to remove it from, the server just checks the signature. That's exactly why refresh tokens exist, and that's tomorrow.*
> *The nice part is that I built the client half of this in October. I'm writing the other end of something I already had to consume."*

**5 từ mới:**

| Từ / cụm | Nghĩa | Câu mẫu |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `roll your own` | tự làm thay vì dùng thư viện | *Rolling your own auth is usually the wrong call.* |
| `up front` | nói rõ ngay từ đầu | *I want to say up front.* |
| `return early` | thoát sớm khỏi hàm | *If you return early, it's faster.* |
| `enumerate users` | liệt kê tài khoản có thật | *An attacker can enumerate your users.* |
| `revoke` (v) | thu hồi | *The access token can't be revoked.* |

